{
  "$comment": "The colour of the sky, the sun and the ambient light through one day, read by BOTH engines: SexyBiscuit.Engine/Rendering/SkyGradient.cs and html5/src/rendering/SkyGradient.js. A day/night cycle is almost entirely colour, and colour written twice is two different dusks -- the desktop build warm and the web build blue, with nothing able to see it. Time runs 0 to 1 with 0 at midnight and 0.5 at noon. Keys are interpolated linearly and the table wraps, so the value at 0.99 blends towards the key at 0.",
  "version": 1,
  "$keyComment": "zenith and horizon paint the sky gradient; sun is the directional light's colour and sunIntensity its strength; ambientSky and ambientGround are the hemisphere ambient; fog is the distance haze and fogDensity how thick it is.",
